<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!-- PRESENT-DAY THREE-ARM EXPERIMENT - CONTROL ARM C-random, DRAW r3, SEED 44

     C-random is the control for arm C. C's ten new sites were placed by greedy
     capacity-aware p-median against the same encampment demand points the run is
     then scored on, so "C beats B" could be partly definitional. This arm is arm C
     with the optimiser switched off and NOTHING else changed:

       * the same 36 real facilities at their real coordinates, expanded x1.5
       * the same ten new sites
       * the SAME per-site capacity vector, copied facility-for-facility from
         arm C's own file (shelters_2026_expanded_plus_new_sites.csv)
       * the same total system capacity, 6,842 - equal to arms B and C
       * the same population, demographics, PM2.5 field, street network and
         opening dates, and every parameter below identical to arm C's file

     ONLY DIFFERENCE: the ten new coordinates are drawn UNIFORMLY AT RANDOM from
     street-graph nodes inside the demand bounding box (largest connected
     component, existing-facility nodes excluded) instead of by p-median.

     Site selection used python random.Random(3) - a FIXED, STATED site-seed,
     separate from and unrelated to randomSeed below, which is the model's own RNG
     seed exactly as in arms A/B/C. Three independent draws (r1/r2/r3) exist so a
     single lucky or unlucky site set cannot be mistaken for a result.

     Built by scripts/build_scenario_crandom_2026.py ->
     data/shelters/shelters_2026_random_sites_r3.csv (46 facilities, 6,842 spaces).

     Interpretation: a B -> C-random gap is DISPERSION (ten extra doors anywhere);
     a C-random -> C gap is OPTIMISATION (choosing where those doors go).

     Population n = 6842 is the 2025 Tri-County Point-in-Time count for
     Multnomah County (PSU HRAC, published 2025-11-04): 10,526 people
     experiencing homelessness, of whom more than 65% were unsheltered.
     The model represents the UNSHELTERED only.

     enableHeterogeneity=1        residents carry sourced age / sex / mobility /
                                  asthma / COPD attributes and walk at their own speed.
     respectShelterOpeningDates=1 shelters open on their real dates (A-02).

     walkingSpeedMps is declared but IGNORED when heterogeneity is on. -->
<sweep runs="1">
	<parameter name="numAgents" type="constant" constant_type="int" value="6842"/>
	<parameter name="randomSeed" type="constant" constant_type="int" value="44"/>
	<parameter name="minutesPerTick" type="constant" constant_type="number" value="1.0"/>
	<parameter name="walkingSpeedMps" type="constant" constant_type="number" value="1.30"/>
	<parameter name="shelterArrivalDistanceM" type="constant" constant_type="number" value="200.0"/>
	<parameter name="evacuationThresholdUgM3" type="constant" constant_type="number" value="55.5"/>
	<parameter name="simulationHours" type="constant" constant_type="int" value="312"/>
	<parameter name="scenarioCode" type="constant" constant_type="int" value="6"/>
	<parameter name="enableHeterogeneity" type="constant" constant_type="int" value="1"/>
	<parameter name="respectShelterOpeningDates" type="constant" constant_type="int" value="1"/>
</sweep>
